  Thread.sleep(usrSleepTime);
</pre>

<b>Example 2:</b> The following code reads a String from a zip file. Because it uses the <code>readLine()</code> method, it will read an unbounded amount of input. An attacker may take advantage of this code to cause an <code>OutOfMemoryException</code> or to consume a large amount of memory so that the program spends more time performing garbage collection or runs out of memory during some subsequent operation.

<pre>
  InputStream zipInput = zipFile.getInputStream(zipEntry);
  Reader zipReader = new InputStreamReader(zipInput);
  BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(zipReader);
  String line = br.readLine();
</pre>

Description.Recommendations:
